    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37736" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praemĭātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		praemior. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A robber</i> (ante-class.), Naev. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 150, 23</span></i> (Com. Rel. p. 6
			Rib.).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A rewarder</i>, <i>one who gives a
				reward to</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luctantium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Psa. 36, 57</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
